window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b180-9ff1fcfa7864c016.json"]={sha256:"9ff1fcfa7864c016d68151ff410a06833e57bec5374219992261f6e635312c7e",value:{"id":"b180","title":"連續壁槽溝穩定","titleEn":"Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"連續壁成槽時，穩定液必須與地下水、土層滲透性及地面載重共同維持槽壁穩定。本課從壓差與濾餅機理出發，連結槽段幾何、垂直度、沉渣與鋼筋籠浮力，再用混凝土量平衡與接頭水力坡降建立施工品質及鄰房變形的驗證鏈。","summaryEn":"During diaphragm-wall excavation, support fluid interacts with groundwater, permeability and surface loading to maintain trench stability. The course connects pressure balance and filter cake to panel geometry, verticality, sediment and cage buoyancy, then uses concrete-volume balance and joint hydraulic gradients to verify construction quality and adjacent-asset movement.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-ground","subcategoryTitle":"地盤改良與地下維護","subcategoryTitleEn":"Ground improvement and underground maintenance","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-ground","learningTags":["underground","ug-ground","ground"],"architectureFamily":"ground","architectureNodes":[["穩定液壓差","Slurry pressure margin"],["濾餅滲流","Filter-cake seepage"],["槽邊載重","Trench-edge surcharge"],["鋼筋籠浮力","Cage buoyancy"],["接頭水力坡降","Joint hydraulic gradient"],["鄰房角變形","Adjacent-building distortion"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[3,0]],"diagram":{"type":"ground","labels":["穩定液壓差","濾餅滲流","槽邊載重","鋼筋籠浮力","接頭水力坡降"],"labelsEn":["Slurry pressure margin","Filter-cake seepage","Trench-edge surcharge","Cage buoyancy","Joint hydraulic gradient"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學例：假設穩定液與地下水液面相同，單位重分別為11與9.81 kN/m³，在深度20 m的靜水壓差為Δp=(11−9.81)×20=23.8 kPa。保持液位與密度條件不變，若檢查深度增加10%至22 m，壓差增為26.18 kPa。這只增加液壓差，不代表整體槽壁安全也增加10%，因為土壓、地層變化及槽段幾何同步影響穩定。應把液位實測、濾餅形成及槽邊載重納入完整分析，再由成槽設計者確認可接受的施工條件。","textEn":"Original teaching example: assume equal slurry and groundwater levels with unit weights of 11 and 9.81 kN/m³. At 20 m depth the static pressure margin is Δp=(11−9.81)×20=23.8 kPa. Holding levels and densities fixed while increasing depth by 10% to 22 m gives 26.18 kPa. This increases hydraulic margin only, not overall trench stability by 10%, because earth pressures, changing strata and panel geometry also influence the mechanism. Include observed fluid levels, filter-cake formation and edge surcharge in the complete analysis before the excavation designer confirms acceptable site-specific construction conditions.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b180-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「穩定液壓差的機理與驗證」與「濾餅滲流的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification\" and \"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b180-v14-01","title":"穩定液壓差的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「穩定液壓差」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Slurry pressure margin” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"穩定液的靜水壓對槽壁施加支承，地下水則從外側抵銷部分壓力，兩者須以同一高程及液面比較。液位突然下降可能使支承消失，密度增加雖可提高壓力，卻也影響沉渣、流動及混凝土置換，不能單獨追求較大數值。壓差不是完整槽壁安全係數，還須檢查土楔、地面載重及三維拱效應；高滲透地層可能無法形成有效壓力邊界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「穩定液壓差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Support-fluid pressure acts on trench walls while external groundwater offsets part of it, requiring comparison at a common elevation and fluid level. A sudden level drop can remove support. Higher density increases pressure but also affects sedimentation, flow and concrete displacement, so maximizing density alone is not a rational criterion. Pressure margin is not a complete trench-stability factor; soil wedges, surcharge and three-dimensional arching also matter, and permeable strata may not sustain the intended pressure boundary. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Slurry pressure margin” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設液面相同、穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、水γw=9.81 kN/m³、深度z=20 m，Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: With equal fluid levels, γs=11 kN/m³, γw=9.81 kN/m³ and z=20 m, Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「穩定液壓差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Slurry pressure margin”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-01-k1","title":"穩定液壓差的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification","text":"穩定液的靜水壓對槽壁施加支承，地下水則從外側抵銷部分壓力，兩者須以同一高程及液面比較。液位突然下降可能使支承消失，密度增加雖可提高壓力，卻也影響沉渣、流動及混凝土置換，不能單獨追求較大數值。","textEn":"Support-fluid pressure acts on trench walls while external groundwater offsets part of it, requiring comparison at a common elevation and fluid level. A sudden level drop can remove support.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「穩定液壓差的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。","穩定液的靜水壓對槽壁施加支承，地下水則從外側抵銷部分壓力，兩者須以同一高程及液面比較。","穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level.","Support-fluid pressure acts on trench walls while external groundwater offsets part of it, requiring comparison at a common elevation and fluid level.","Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil."],"answer":1,"explanation":"穩定液的靜水壓對槽壁施加支承，地下水則從外側抵銷部分壓力，兩者須以同一高程及液面比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Support-fluid pressure acts on trench walls while external groundwater offsets part of it, requiring comparison at a common elevation and fluid level. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b180-v14-02","title":"穩定液壓差的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「穩定液壓差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Slurry pressure margin” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設液面相同、穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、水γw=9.81 kN/m³、深度z=20 m，Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: With equal fluid levels, γs=11 kN/m³, γw=9.81 kN/m³ and z=20 m, Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分深度測密度並連續追蹤液位，對照外側水壓計；將液位差與密度差分開帶入壓力圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure density by depth and continuously track fluid level against external piezometers, separating level and density differences in pressure diagrams.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設液面相同、穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、水γw=9.81 kN/m³、深度z=20 m，Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: With equal fluid levels, γs=11 kN/m³, γw=9.81 kN/m³ and z=20 m, Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「穩定液壓差的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。","清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。","原創教學假設：假設液面相同、穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、水γw=9.81 kN/m³、深度z=20 m，Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa。"],"optionsEn":["No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability.","Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement.","Original teaching assumptions: With equal fluid levels, γs=11 kN/m³, γw=9.81 kN/m³ and z=20 m, Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設液面相同、穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、水γw=9.81 kN/m³、深度z=20 m，Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: With equal fluid levels, γs=11 kN/m³, γw=9.81 kN/m³ and z=20 m, Δp=(γs−γw)z=23.8 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b180-v14-03","title":"穩定液壓差的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「穩定液壓差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Slurry pressure margin” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分深度測密度並連續追蹤液位，對照外側水壓計；將液位差與密度差分開帶入壓力圖。每個槽段應保留液位與密度時間線；異常漏失的停留點由成槽及地工負責人共同確認。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure density by depth and continuously track fluid level against external piezometers, separating level and density differences in pressure diagrams. Retain fluid-level and density time histories for every panel; excavation and geotechnical leads jointly confirm hold points for abnormal fluid loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每個槽段應保留液位與密度時間線；異常漏失的停留點由成槽及地工負責人共同確認。壓差不是完整槽壁安全係數，還須檢查土楔、地面載重及三維拱效應；高滲透地層可能無法形成有效壓力邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Retain fluid-level and density time histories for every panel; excavation and geotechnical leads jointly confirm hold points for abnormal fluid loss. Pressure margin is not a complete trench-stability factor; soil wedges, surcharge and three-dimensional arching also matter, and permeable strata may not sustain the intended pressure boundary.","failure":"注意干擾：穩定液漏失會降低支承壓力，槽口沉陷或局部坍塌可能在平均密度仍合格時發生。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fluid loss reduces support pressure; collar settlement or local collapse can occur even while average slurry density remains acceptable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分深度測密度並連續追蹤液位，對照外側水壓計；將液位差與密度差分開帶入壓力圖。每個槽段應保留液位與密度時間線；異常漏失的停留點由成槽及地工負責人共同確認。","textEn":"Measure density by depth and continuously track fluid level against external piezometers, separating level and density differences in pressure diagrams. Retain fluid-level and density time histories for every panel; excavation and geotechnical leads jointly confirm hold points for abnormal fluid loss.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每個槽段應保留液位與密度時間線；異常漏失的停留點由成槽及地工負責人共同確認。壓差不是完整槽壁安全係數，還須檢查土楔、地面載重及三維拱效應；高滲透地層可能無法形成有效壓力邊界。","textEn":"Retain fluid-level and density time histories for every panel; excavation and geotechnical leads jointly confirm hold points for abnormal fluid loss. Pressure margin is not a complete trench-stability factor; soil wedges, surcharge and three-dimensional arching also matter, and permeable strata may not sustain the intended pressure boundary.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「穩定液壓差的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification\"?","options":["分深度測密度並連續追蹤液位，對照外側水壓計；將液位差與密度差分開帶入壓力圖。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。"],"optionsEn":["Measure density by depth and continuously track fluid level against external piezometers, separating level and density differences in pressure diagrams.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分深度測密度並連續追蹤液位，對照外側水壓計；將液位差與密度差分開帶入壓力圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure density by depth and continuously track fluid level against external piezometers, separating level and density differences in pressure diagrams. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b180-v14-04","title":"穩定液壓差的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「穩定液壓差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Slurry pressure margin” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"穩定液漏失會降低支承壓力，槽口沉陷或局部坍塌可能在平均密度仍合格時發生。壓差不是完整槽壁安全係數，還須檢查土楔、地面載重及三維拱效應；高滲透地層可能無法形成有效壓力邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fluid loss reduces support pressure; collar settlement or local collapse can occur even while average slurry density remains acceptable. Pressure margin is not a complete trench-stability factor; soil wedges, surcharge and three-dimensional arching also matter, and permeable strata may not sustain the intended pressure boundary. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：壓差不是完整槽壁安全係數，還須檢查土楔、地面載重及三維拱效應；高滲透地層可能無法形成有效壓力邊界。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pressure margin is not a complete trench-stability factor; soil wedges, surcharge and three-dimensional arching also matter, and permeable strata may not sustain the intended pressure boundary.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"穩定液漏失會降低支承壓力，槽口沉陷或局部坍塌可能在平均密度仍合格時發生。壓差不是完整槽壁安全係數，還須檢查土楔、地面載重及三維拱效應；高滲透地層可能無法形成有效壓力邊界。","textEn":"Fluid loss reduces support pressure; collar settlement or local collapse can occur even while average slurry density remains acceptable. Pressure margin is not a complete trench-stability factor; soil wedges, surcharge and three-dimensional arching also matter, and permeable strata may not sustain the intended pressure boundary.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「穩定液壓差的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Slurry pressure margin mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","穩定液漏失會降低支承壓力，槽口沉陷或局部坍塌可能在平均密度仍合格時發生。","穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Fluid loss reduces support pressure; collar settlement or local collapse can occur even while average slurry density remains acceptable.","Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil."],"answer":1,"explanation":"穩定液漏失會降低支承壓力，槽口沉陷或局部坍塌可能在平均密度仍合格時發生。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fluid loss reduces support pressure; collar settlement or local collapse can occur even while average slurry density remains acceptable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b180-v14-05","title":"濾餅滲流的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「濾餅滲流」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Filter-cake seepage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"穩定液在可滲透槽壁形成低滲透濾餅，才可把液壓有效傳給土骨架；若濾餅太薄、破損或無法形成，液體可能深入地層而失去支承效果。濾餅厚度也影響後續混凝土與土體接觸，成槽穩定與接面品質不能分開看。式中流速是達西通量而非孔隙內真實流速，假設均勻完整濾餅；開裂及粗孔隙穿透不能靠此一維模型表達。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「濾餅滲流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A low-permeability filter cake allows slurry pressure to act effectively on the soil skeleton. Thin, damaged or absent cake permits fluid penetration and loss of support efficiency. Cake thickness also affects later concrete-ground contact, linking excavation stability with interface quality rather than treating them as unrelated controls. The velocity is Darcy flux rather than pore-water velocity and assumes intact uniform cake; cracking and penetration into coarse voids fall outside this one-dimensional model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filter-cake seepage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設濾餅k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、水頭差Δh=10 m、厚度t=0.005 m，達西流速v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For cake permeability k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s, head difference Δh=10 m and thickness t=0.005 m, Darcy flux v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「濾餅滲流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filter-cake seepage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-05-k1","title":"濾餅滲流的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification","text":"穩定液在可滲透槽壁形成低滲透濾餅，才可把液壓有效傳給土骨架；若濾餅太薄、破損或無法形成，液體可能深入地層而失去支承效果。濾餅厚度也影響後續混凝土與土體接觸，成槽穩定與接面品質不能分開看。","textEn":"A low-permeability filter cake allows slurry pressure to act effectively on the soil skeleton. Thin, damaged or absent cake permits fluid penetration and loss of support efficiency.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「濾餅滲流的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。","槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。","穩定液在可滲透槽壁形成低滲透濾餅，才可把液壓有效傳給土骨架；若濾餅太薄、破損或無法形成，液體可能深入地層而失去支承效果。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil.","Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety.","A low-permeability filter cake allows slurry pressure to act effectively on the soil skeleton."],"answer":2,"explanation":"穩定液在可滲透槽壁形成低滲透濾餅，才可把液壓有效傳給土骨架；若濾餅太薄、破損或無法形成，液體可能深入地層而失去支承效果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A low-permeability filter cake allows slurry pressure to act effectively on the soil skeleton. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b180-v14-06","title":"濾餅滲流的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濾餅滲流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Filter-cake seepage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設濾餅k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、水頭差Δh=10 m、厚度t=0.005 m，達西流速v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For cake permeability k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s, head difference Δh=10 m and thickness t=0.005 m, Darcy flux v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以濾失與泥皮試驗配合地層粒徑判斷濾餅形成，核對現場液位補充量及漏失位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use fluid-loss and cake tests with soil grading to assess cake formation, checking field replenishment volumes and fluid-loss locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設濾餅k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、水頭差Δh=10 m、厚度t=0.005 m，達西流速v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For cake permeability k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s, head difference Δh=10 m and thickness t=0.005 m, Darcy flux v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「濾餅滲流的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設濾餅k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、水頭差Δh=10 m、厚度t=0.005 m，達西流速v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s。","槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。","鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For cake permeability k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s, head difference Δh=10 m and thickness t=0.005 m, Darcy flux v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s.","A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position.","Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設濾餅k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、水頭差Δh=10 m、厚度t=0.005 m，達西流速v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For cake permeability k=1×10⁻⁹ m/s, head difference Δh=10 m and thickness t=0.005 m, Darcy flux v=kΔh/t=2×10⁻⁶ m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b180-v14-07","title":"濾餅滲流的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「濾餅滲流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filter-cake seepage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以濾失與泥皮試驗配合地層粒徑判斷濾餅形成，核對現場液位補充量及漏失位置。穩定液配方試驗需對應代表性地層；漏失機理未辨明前，地工設計者應審查替代支承或預處理方案。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use fluid-loss and cake tests with soil grading to assess cake formation, checking field replenishment volumes and fluid-loss locations. Fluid qualification must represent the ground; before proceeding with unexplained losses, the geotechnical designer reviews alternative support or pretreatment options. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：穩定液配方試驗需對應代表性地層；漏失機理未辨明前，地工設計者應審查替代支承或預處理方案。式中流速是達西通量而非孔隙內真實流速，假設均勻完整濾餅；開裂及粗孔隙穿透不能靠此一維模型表達。","observationEn":"Site practice: Fluid qualification must represent the ground; before proceeding with unexplained losses, the geotechnical designer reviews alternative support or pretreatment options. The velocity is Darcy flux rather than pore-water velocity and assumes intact uniform cake; cracking and penetration into coarse voids fall outside this one-dimensional model.","failure":"注意干擾：把試驗杯內泥皮表現直接套用於礫石層，可能漏掉大孔隙流失與槽壁局部失穩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Transferring laboratory filter-cake behaviour directly to gravel may miss large-pore fluid loss and local wall instability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以濾失與泥皮試驗配合地層粒徑判斷濾餅形成，核對現場液位補充量及漏失位置。穩定液配方試驗需對應代表性地層；漏失機理未辨明前，地工設計者應審查替代支承或預處理方案。","textEn":"Use fluid-loss and cake tests with soil grading to assess cake formation, checking field replenishment volumes and fluid-loss locations. Fluid qualification must represent the ground; before proceeding with unexplained losses, the geotechnical designer reviews alternative support or pretreatment options.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"穩定液配方試驗需對應代表性地層；漏失機理未辨明前，地工設計者應審查替代支承或預處理方案。式中流速是達西通量而非孔隙內真實流速，假設均勻完整濾餅；開裂及粗孔隙穿透不能靠此一維模型表達。","textEn":"Fluid qualification must represent the ground; before proceeding with unexplained losses, the geotechnical designer reviews alternative support or pretreatment options. The velocity is Darcy flux rather than pore-water velocity and assumes intact uniform cake; cracking and penetration into coarse voids fall outside this one-dimensional model.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「濾餅滲流的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以濾失與泥皮試驗配合地層粒徑判斷濾餅形成，核對現場液位補充量及漏失位置。","連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Use fluid-loss and cake tests with soil grading to assess cake formation, checking field replenishment volumes and fluid-loss locations.","Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以濾失與泥皮試驗配合地層粒徑判斷濾餅形成，核對現場液位補充量及漏失位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use fluid-loss and cake tests with soil grading to assess cake formation, checking field replenishment volumes and fluid-loss locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b180-v14-08","title":"濾餅滲流的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濾餅滲流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Filter-cake seepage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把試驗杯內泥皮表現直接套用於礫石層，可能漏掉大孔隙流失與槽壁局部失穩。式中流速是達西通量而非孔隙內真實流速，假設均勻完整濾餅；開裂及粗孔隙穿透不能靠此一維模型表達。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Transferring laboratory filter-cake behaviour directly to gravel may miss large-pore fluid loss and local wall instability. The velocity is Darcy flux rather than pore-water velocity and assumes intact uniform cake; cracking and penetration into coarse voids fall outside this one-dimensional model. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：式中流速是達西通量而非孔隙內真實流速，假設均勻完整濾餅；開裂及粗孔隙穿透不能靠此一維模型表達。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The velocity is Darcy flux rather than pore-water velocity and assumes intact uniform cake; cracking and penetration into coarse voids fall outside this one-dimensional model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把試驗杯內泥皮表現直接套用於礫石層，可能漏掉大孔隙流失與槽壁局部失穩。式中流速是達西通量而非孔隙內真實流速，假設均勻完整濾餅；開裂及粗孔隙穿透不能靠此一維模型表達。","textEn":"Transferring laboratory filter-cake behaviour directly to gravel may miss large-pore fluid loss and local wall instability. The velocity is Darcy flux rather than pore-water velocity and assumes intact uniform cake; cracking and penetration into coarse voids fall outside this one-dimensional model.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「濾餅滲流的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Filter-cake seepage mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。","把試驗杯內泥皮表現直接套用於礫石層，可能漏掉大孔隙流失與槽壁局部失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety.","Transferring laboratory filter-cake behaviour directly to gravel may miss large-pore fluid loss and local wall instability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把試驗杯內泥皮表現直接套用於礫石層，可能漏掉大孔隙流失與槽壁局部失穩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Transferring laboratory filter-cake behaviour directly to gravel may miss large-pore fluid loss and local wall instability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b180-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「槽段三維效應的機理與驗證」與「槽邊載重的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification\" and \"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b180-v14-09","title":"槽段三維效應的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「槽段三維效應」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Panel three-dimensional effect” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"有限槽段的兩端土體可提供三維拱效應，因而槽長與深度會影響穩定，不能把無限長剖面的結果無條件套用。延長槽段可減少接頭數，卻增加開放面與施工時間，也可能穿越更多地層變異，方案取捨需要同時考量。長深比僅為幾何描述，並無通用允收界限；完整分析仍需土體強度、液壓、地面載重與槽端條件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「槽段三維效應」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Soil at the ends of a finite panel provides three-dimensional arching, making stability sensitive to panel length and depth. An infinite-section result cannot be transferred unconditionally. Longer panels reduce joint count but enlarge exposure, prolong excavation and cross more ground variability, so these effects must be considered together. The length-depth ratio describes geometry and has no universal acceptance threshold; full analysis still needs soil strength, fluid pressure, surcharge and end conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Panel three-dimensional effect” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設槽段長L=6 m、深H=30 m，幾何比L/H=0.20。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For panel length L=6 m and depth H=30 m, the geometric ratio L/H=0.20.","failure":"常見誤解：「槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「槽段三維效應」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Panel three-dimensional effect”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-09-k1","title":"槽段三維效應的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification","text":"有限槽段的兩端土體可提供三維拱效應，因而槽長與深度會影響穩定，不能把無限長剖面的結果無條件套用。延長槽段可減少接頭數，卻增加開放面與施工時間，也可能穿越更多地層變異，方案取捨需要同時考量。","textEn":"Soil at the ends of a finite panel provides three-dimensional arching, making stability sensitive to panel length and depth. An infinite-section result cannot be transferred unconditionally.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「槽段三維效應的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["有限槽段的兩端土體可提供三維拱效應，因而槽長與深度會影響穩定，不能把無限長剖面的結果無條件套用。","槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。","地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Soil at the ends of a finite panel provides three-dimensional arching, making stability sensitive to panel length and depth.","Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety.","No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"有限槽段的兩端土體可提供三維拱效應，因而槽長與深度會影響穩定，不能把無限長剖面的結果無條件套用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Soil at the ends of a finite panel provides three-dimensional arching, making stability sensitive to panel length and depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b180-v14-10","title":"槽段三維效應的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「槽段三維效應」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Panel three-dimensional effect” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設槽段長L=6 m、深H=30 m，幾何比L/H=0.20。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For panel length L=6 m and depth H=30 m, the geometric ratio L/H=0.20. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對各槽長方案建立相同地層及液壓邊界，核對端部與中段變形；把實際開放時間列入比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare panel-length options under the same ground and fluid-pressure boundaries, checking end and mid-panel movement and including actual exposure duration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設槽段長L=6 m、深H=30 m，幾何比L/H=0.20。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For panel length L=6 m and depth H=30 m, the geometric ratio L/H=0.20. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「槽段三維效應的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。","原創教學假設：假設槽段長L=6 m、深H=30 m，幾何比L/H=0.20。","混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。"],"optionsEn":["Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement.","Original teaching assumptions: For panel length L=6 m and depth H=30 m, the geometric ratio L/H=0.20.","Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設槽段長L=6 m、深H=30 m，幾何比L/H=0.20。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For panel length L=6 m and depth H=30 m, the geometric ratio L/H=0.20. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b180-v14-11","title":"槽段三維效應的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「槽段三維效應」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Panel three-dimensional effect” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對各槽長方案建立相同地層及液壓邊界，核對端部與中段變形；把實際開放時間列入比較。槽段劃分應與地質剖面及設備能力一併核定；跨越異常地層時，由成槽設計者重審槽長而非照抄標準分段。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare panel-length options under the same ground and fluid-pressure boundaries, checking end and mid-panel movement and including actual exposure duration. Approve panel layout with geology and equipment capability; the excavation designer reassesses length across anomalous ground rather than repeating a standard panel arrangement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：槽段劃分應與地質剖面及設備能力一併核定；跨越異常地層時，由成槽設計者重審槽長而非照抄標準分段。長深比僅為幾何描述，並無通用允收界限；完整分析仍需土體強度、液壓、地面載重與槽端條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Approve panel layout with geology and equipment capability; the excavation designer reassesses length across anomalous ground rather than repeating a standard panel arrangement. The length-depth ratio describes geometry and has no universal acceptance threshold; full analysis still needs soil strength, fluid pressure, surcharge and end conditions.","failure":"注意干擾：長槽段若跨越局部軟弱層，端部拱效應可能不足，槽壁變形與超挖會先集中於中段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A long panel crossing a weak lens may gain insufficient end restraint, concentrating deformation and overbreak near the middle. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對各槽長方案建立相同地層及液壓邊界，核對端部與中段變形；把實際開放時間列入比較。槽段劃分應與地質剖面及設備能力一併核定；跨越異常地層時，由成槽設計者重審槽長而非照抄標準分段。","textEn":"Compare panel-length options under the same ground and fluid-pressure boundaries, checking end and mid-panel movement and including actual exposure duration. Approve panel layout with geology and equipment capability; the excavation designer reassesses length across anomalous ground rather than repeating a standard panel arrangement.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"槽段劃分應與地質剖面及設備能力一併核定；跨越異常地層時，由成槽設計者重審槽長而非照抄標準分段。長深比僅為幾何描述，並無通用允收界限；完整分析仍需土體強度、液壓、地面載重與槽端條件。","textEn":"Approve panel layout with geology and equipment capability; the excavation designer reassesses length across anomalous ground rather than repeating a standard panel arrangement. The length-depth ratio describes geometry and has no universal acceptance threshold; full analysis still needs soil strength, fluid pressure, surcharge and end conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「槽段三維效應的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。","對各槽長方案建立相同地層及液壓邊界，核對端部與中段變形；把實際開放時間列入比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members.","Compare panel-length options under the same ground and fluid-pressure boundaries, checking end and mid-panel movement and including actual exposure duration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對各槽長方案建立相同地層及液壓邊界，核對端部與中段變形；把實際開放時間列入比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare panel-length options under the same ground and fluid-pressure boundaries, checking end and mid-panel movement and including actual exposure duration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b180-v14-12","title":"槽段三維效應的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「槽段三維效應」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Panel three-dimensional effect” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"長槽段若跨越局部軟弱層，端部拱效應可能不足，槽壁變形與超挖會先集中於中段。長深比僅為幾何描述，並無通用允收界限；完整分析仍需土體強度、液壓、地面載重與槽端條件。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A long panel crossing a weak lens may gain insufficient end restraint, concentrating deformation and overbreak near the middle. The length-depth ratio describes geometry and has no universal acceptance threshold; full analysis still needs soil strength, fluid pressure, surcharge and end conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：長深比僅為幾何描述，並無通用允收界限；完整分析仍需土體強度、液壓、地面載重與槽端條件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The length-depth ratio describes geometry and has no universal acceptance threshold; full analysis still needs soil strength, fluid pressure, surcharge and end conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"長槽段若跨越局部軟弱層，端部拱效應可能不足，槽壁變形與超挖會先集中於中段。長深比僅為幾何描述，並無通用允收界限；完整分析仍需土體強度、液壓、地面載重與槽端條件。","textEn":"A long panel crossing a weak lens may gain insufficient end restraint, concentrating deformation and overbreak near the middle. The length-depth ratio describes geometry and has no universal acceptance threshold; full analysis still needs soil strength, fluid pressure, surcharge and end conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「槽段三維效應的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Panel three-dimensional effect mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["長槽段若跨越局部軟弱層，端部拱效應可能不足，槽壁變形與超挖會先集中於中段。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。"],"optionsEn":["A long panel crossing a weak lens may gain insufficient end restraint, concentrating deformation and overbreak near the middle.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"長槽段若跨越局部軟弱層，端部拱效應可能不足，槽壁變形與超挖會先集中於中段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A long panel crossing a weak lens may gain insufficient end restraint, concentrating deformation and overbreak near the middle. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b180-v14-13","title":"槽邊載重的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「槽邊載重」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Trench-edge surcharge” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"吊車、履帶機及材料堆置增加槽邊土體的側向需求，作用不一定均勻，也會隨機具移動而改變。簡化側壓係數可說明均布附加載重的量級，但局部履帶及支腿作用需按距離與接地範圍分析，不能只用全場平均荷重。側壓係數須對應土體狀態及允許變形，局部載重還有三維擴散；本式不是吊車站位或支腿操作許可。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「槽邊載重」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cranes, tracked machinery and stockpiles increase lateral demand near the trench, with nonuniform effects that change as equipment moves. A pressure coefficient illustrates a uniform surcharge scale, but tracks and outriggers require analysis by distance and contact area rather than a site-wide average load. The coefficient must match soil state and permitted movement, while local loads spread in three dimensions; this equation does not authorize crane positioning or outrigger operations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Trench-edge surcharge” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設均布附加載重q=40 kPa、側壓係數K=0.5，增量Δσh=Kq=20 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For uniform surcharge q=40 kPa and lateral coefficient K=0.5, incremental pressure Δσh=Kq=20 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「槽邊載重」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Trench-edge surcharge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-13-k1","title":"槽邊載重的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification","text":"吊車、履帶機及材料堆置增加槽邊土體的側向需求，作用不一定均勻，也會隨機具移動而改變。簡化側壓係數可說明均布附加載重的量級，但局部履帶及支腿作用需按距離與接地範圍分析，不能只用全場平均荷重。","textEn":"Cranes, tracked machinery and stockpiles increase lateral demand near the trench, with nonuniform effects that change as equipment moves. A pressure coefficient illustrates a uniform surcharge scale, but tracks and outriggers require analysis by distance and contact area rather than a site-wide average load.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「槽邊載重的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。","吊車、履帶機及材料堆置增加槽邊土體的側向需求，作用不一定均勻，也會隨機具移動而改變。","槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。"],"optionsEn":["No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability.","Cranes, tracked machinery and stockpiles increase lateral demand near the trench, with nonuniform effects that change as equipment moves.","A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"吊車、履帶機及材料堆置增加槽邊土體的側向需求，作用不一定均勻，也會隨機具移動而改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cranes, tracked machinery and stockpiles increase lateral demand near the trench, with nonuniform effects that change as equipment moves. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b180-v14-14","title":"槽邊載重的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「槽邊載重」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Trench-edge surcharge” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設均布附加載重q=40 kPa、側壓係數K=0.5，增量Δσh=Kq=20 kPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For uniform surcharge q=40 kPa and lateral coefficient K=0.5, incremental pressure Δσh=Kq=20 kPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對機具位置、接地尺寸及堆料高度，將實際載重位置投影到槽壁分析，不以道路容許載重替代。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check machine locations, contact dimensions and stockpile heights, projecting actual loads into trench analysis rather than substituting a road-load rating.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設均布附加載重q=40 kPa、側壓係數K=0.5，增量Δσh=Kq=20 kPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For uniform surcharge q=40 kPa and lateral coefficient K=0.5, incremental pressure Δσh=Kq=20 kPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「槽邊載重的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。","連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。","原創教學假設：假設均布附加載重q=40 kPa、側壓係數K=0.5，增量Δσh=Kq=20 kPa。"],"optionsEn":["Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction.","Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight.","Original teaching assumptions: For uniform surcharge q=40 kPa and lateral coefficient K=0.5, incremental pressure Δσh=Kq=20 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設均布附加載重q=40 kPa、側壓係數K=0.5，增量Δσh=Kq=20 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For uniform surcharge q=40 kPa and lateral coefficient K=0.5, incremental pressure Δσh=Kq=20 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b180-v14-15","title":"槽邊載重的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「槽邊載重」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Trench-edge surcharge” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對機具位置、接地尺寸及堆料高度，將實際載重位置投影到槽壁分析，不以道路容許載重替代。成槽平面圖需標出載重控制區與機具移位條件；臨時工程設計者核准後才調整吊裝站位。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check machine locations, contact dimensions and stockpile heights, projecting actual loads into trench analysis rather than substituting a road-load rating. The excavation plan identifies load-control zones and relocation conditions; the temporary-works designer approves changes before lifting positions move. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：成槽平面圖需標出載重控制區與機具移位條件；臨時工程設計者核准後才調整吊裝站位。側壓係數須對應土體狀態及允許變形，局部載重還有三維擴散；本式不是吊車站位或支腿操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: The excavation plan identifies load-control zones and relocation conditions; the temporary-works designer approves changes before lifting positions move. The coefficient must match soil state and permitted movement, while local loads spread in three dimensions; this equation does not authorize crane positioning or outrigger operations.","failure":"注意干擾：吊車靠近槽邊或支腿反力集中會提高局部側壓，造成地面裂縫與穩定液漏失的連鎖反應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A crane close to the edge or concentrated outrigger reaction can raise local lateral pressure, initiating ground cracking and subsequent slurry loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對機具位置、接地尺寸及堆料高度，將實際載重位置投影到槽壁分析，不以道路容許載重替代。成槽平面圖需標出載重控制區與機具移位條件；臨時工程設計者核准後才調整吊裝站位。","textEn":"Check machine locations, contact dimensions and stockpile heights, projecting actual loads into trench analysis rather than substituting a road-load rating. The excavation plan identifies load-control zones and relocation conditions; the temporary-works designer approves changes before lifting positions move.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"成槽平面圖需標出載重控制區與機具移位條件；臨時工程設計者核准後才調整吊裝站位。側壓係數須對應土體狀態及允許變形，局部載重還有三維擴散；本式不是吊車站位或支腿操作許可。","textEn":"The excavation plan identifies load-control zones and relocation conditions; the temporary-works designer approves changes before lifting positions move. The coefficient must match soil state and permitted movement, while local loads spread in three dimensions; this equation does not authorize crane positioning or outrigger operations.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「槽邊載重的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對機具位置、接地尺寸及堆料高度，將實際載重位置投影到槽壁分析，不以道路容許載重替代。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。"],"optionsEn":["Check machine locations, contact dimensions and stockpile heights, projecting actual loads into trench analysis rather than substituting a road-load rating.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對機具位置、接地尺寸及堆料高度，將實際載重位置投影到槽壁分析，不以道路容許載重替代。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check machine locations, contact dimensions and stockpile heights, projecting actual loads into trench analysis rather than substituting a road-load rating. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b180-v14-16","title":"槽邊載重的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「槽邊載重」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Trench-edge surcharge” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"吊車靠近槽邊或支腿反力集中會提高局部側壓，造成地面裂縫與穩定液漏失的連鎖反應。側壓係數須對應土體狀態及允許變形，局部載重還有三維擴散；本式不是吊車站位或支腿操作許可。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A crane close to the edge or concentrated outrigger reaction can raise local lateral pressure, initiating ground cracking and subsequent slurry loss. The coefficient must match soil state and permitted movement, while local loads spread in three dimensions; this equation does not authorize crane positioning or outrigger operations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：側壓係數須對應土體狀態及允許變形，局部載重還有三維擴散；本式不是吊車站位或支腿操作許可。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The coefficient must match soil state and permitted movement, while local loads spread in three dimensions; this equation does not authorize crane positioning or outrigger operations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"吊車靠近槽邊或支腿反力集中會提高局部側壓，造成地面裂縫與穩定液漏失的連鎖反應。側壓係數須對應土體狀態及允許變形，局部載重還有三維擴散；本式不是吊車站位或支腿操作許可。","textEn":"A crane close to the edge or concentrated outrigger reaction can raise local lateral pressure, initiating ground cracking and subsequent slurry loss. The coefficient must match soil state and permitted movement, while local loads spread in three dimensions; this equation does not authorize crane positioning or outrigger operations.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「槽邊載重的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Trench-edge surcharge mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","吊車靠近槽邊或支腿反力集中會提高局部側壓，造成地面裂縫與穩定液漏失的連鎖反應。","槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A crane close to the edge or concentrated outrigger reaction can raise local lateral pressure, initiating ground cracking and subsequent slurry loss.","A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"吊車靠近槽邊或支腿反力集中會提高局部側壓，造成地面裂縫與穩定液漏失的連鎖反應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A crane close to the edge or concentrated outrigger reaction can raise local lateral pressure, initiating ground cracking and subsequent slurry loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b180-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「垂直度偏差的機理與驗證」與「槽底沉渣的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification\" and \"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b180-v14-17","title":"垂直度偏差的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「垂直度偏差」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Verticality deviation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"連續壁槽孔偏斜會影響壁厚、鋼筋籠淨距與相鄰槽段接合。深度越大，同樣角度或比例偏差形成的底部偏移越大，兩側槽段若朝相反方向偏離，接頭處的有效重疊可能比單段誤差更不利。此式為固定偏斜的線性估算，真實彎曲孔形須用全深量測；設計接頭能力需採兩槽相對位置，不能只看各自合格率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「垂直度偏差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Trench deviation affects wall thickness, cage clearance and neighbouring-panel connection. At greater depth, the same inclination produces a larger toe offset. Adjacent panels deviating in opposite directions can reduce effective joint overlap more severely than either panel's individual tolerance suggests. This linear estimate assumes constant inclination; a curved trench requires full-depth measurement, and joint performance depends on relative panel positions rather than individual compliance rates. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Verticality deviation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：深度H=40 m、假設偏斜比i=0.005，底部偏移δ=Hi=0.20 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For depth H=40 m and assumed inclination ratio i=0.005, toe offset δ=Hi=0.20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「垂直度偏差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Verticality deviation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-17-k1","title":"垂直度偏差的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification","text":"連續壁槽孔偏斜會影響壁厚、鋼筋籠淨距與相鄰槽段接合。深度越大，同樣角度或比例偏差形成的底部偏移越大，兩側槽段若朝相反方向偏離，接頭處的有效重疊可能比單段誤差更不利。","textEn":"Trench deviation affects wall thickness, cage clearance and neighbouring-panel connection. At greater depth, the same inclination produces a larger toe offset.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「垂直度偏差的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。","清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。","連續壁槽孔偏斜會影響壁厚、鋼筋籠淨距與相鄰槽段接合。"],"optionsEn":["A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position.","Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement.","Trench deviation affects wall thickness, cage clearance and neighbouring-panel connection."],"answer":2,"explanation":"連續壁槽孔偏斜會影響壁厚、鋼筋籠淨距與相鄰槽段接合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Trench deviation affects wall thickness, cage clearance and neighbouring-panel connection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b180-v14-18","title":"垂直度偏差的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「垂直度偏差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Verticality deviation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：深度H=40 m、假設偏斜比i=0.005，底部偏移δ=Hi=0.20 m。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For depth H=40 m and assumed inclination ratio i=0.005, toe offset δ=Hi=0.20 m. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用槽壁超音波量測沿深度的輪廓，核對導牆基準與設備姿態，將相鄰槽段放在同一座標比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use ultrasonic trench profiling by depth, check guide-wall datum and equipment attitude, and compare adjacent panels in one coordinate frame.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：深度H=40 m、假設偏斜比i=0.005，底部偏移δ=Hi=0.20 m。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For depth H=40 m and assumed inclination ratio i=0.005, toe offset δ=Hi=0.20 m. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「垂直度偏差的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：深度H=40 m、假設偏斜比i=0.005，底部偏移δ=Hi=0.20 m。","混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。","建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For depth H=40 m and assumed inclination ratio i=0.005, toe offset δ=Hi=0.20 m.","Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall.","Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：深度H=40 m、假設偏斜比i=0.005，底部偏移δ=Hi=0.20 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For depth H=40 m and assumed inclination ratio i=0.005, toe offset δ=Hi=0.20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b180-v14-19","title":"垂直度偏差的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「垂直度偏差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Verticality deviation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用槽壁超音波量測沿深度的輪廓，核對導牆基準與設備姿態，將相鄰槽段放在同一座標比較。吊放鋼筋籠前應取得全深輪廓驗收；超差位置由壁體設計者核定修正，不以強行下放解決。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use ultrasonic trench profiling by depth, check guide-wall datum and equipment attitude, and compare adjacent panels in one coordinate frame. Obtain full-depth profile acceptance before cage installation; the wall designer approves correction of deviations rather than resolving them by forced placement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：吊放鋼筋籠前應取得全深輪廓驗收；超差位置由壁體設計者核定修正，不以強行下放解決。此式為固定偏斜的線性估算，真實彎曲孔形須用全深量測；設計接頭能力需採兩槽相對位置，不能只看各自合格率。","observationEn":"Site practice: Obtain full-depth profile acceptance before cage installation; the wall designer approves correction of deviations rather than resolving them by forced placement. This linear estimate assumes constant inclination; a curved trench requires full-depth measurement, and joint performance depends on relative panel positions rather than individual compliance rates.","failure":"注意干擾：偏斜可能使鋼筋籠卡住或接頭形成缺口，後續即使灌足混凝土仍無法恢復原設計連續性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Deviation can trap the cage or leave a joint gap; placing the specified concrete volume does not restore the intended continuity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用槽壁超音波量測沿深度的輪廓，核對導牆基準與設備姿態，將相鄰槽段放在同一座標比較。吊放鋼筋籠前應取得全深輪廓驗收；超差位置由壁體設計者核定修正，不以強行下放解決。","textEn":"Use ultrasonic trench profiling by depth, check guide-wall datum and equipment attitude, and compare adjacent panels in one coordinate frame. Obtain full-depth profile acceptance before cage installation; the wall designer approves correction of deviations rather than resolving them by forced placement.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"吊放鋼筋籠前應取得全深輪廓驗收；超差位置由壁體設計者核定修正，不以強行下放解決。此式為固定偏斜的線性估算，真實彎曲孔形須用全深量測；設計接頭能力需採兩槽相對位置，不能只看各自合格率。","textEn":"Obtain full-depth profile acceptance before cage installation; the wall designer approves correction of deviations rather than resolving them by forced placement. This linear estimate assumes constant inclination; a curved trench requires full-depth measurement, and joint performance depends on relative panel positions rather than individual compliance rates.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「垂直度偏差的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用槽壁超音波量測沿深度的輪廓，核對導牆基準與設備姿態，將相鄰槽段放在同一座標比較。","穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use ultrasonic trench profiling by depth, check guide-wall datum and equipment attitude, and compare adjacent panels in one coordinate frame.","Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用槽壁超音波量測沿深度的輪廓，核對導牆基準與設備姿態，將相鄰槽段放在同一座標比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use ultrasonic trench profiling by depth, check guide-wall datum and equipment attitude, and compare adjacent panels in one coordinate frame. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b180-v14-20","title":"垂直度偏差的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「垂直度偏差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Verticality deviation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"偏斜可能使鋼筋籠卡住或接頭形成缺口，後續即使灌足混凝土仍無法恢復原設計連續性。此式為固定偏斜的線性估算，真實彎曲孔形須用全深量測；設計接頭能力需採兩槽相對位置，不能只看各自合格率。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Deviation can trap the cage or leave a joint gap; placing the specified concrete volume does not restore the intended continuity. This linear estimate assumes constant inclination; a curved trench requires full-depth measurement, and joint performance depends on relative panel positions rather than individual compliance rates. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此式為固定偏斜的線性估算，真實彎曲孔形須用全深量測；設計接頭能力需採兩槽相對位置，不能只看各自合格率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This linear estimate assumes constant inclination; a curved trench requires full-depth measurement, and joint performance depends on relative panel positions rather than individual compliance rates.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"偏斜可能使鋼筋籠卡住或接頭形成缺口，後續即使灌足混凝土仍無法恢復原設計連續性。此式為固定偏斜的線性估算，真實彎曲孔形須用全深量測；設計接頭能力需採兩槽相對位置，不能只看各自合格率。","textEn":"Deviation can trap the cage or leave a joint gap; placing the specified concrete volume does not restore the intended continuity. This linear estimate assumes constant inclination; a curved trench requires full-depth measurement, and joint performance depends on relative panel positions rather than individual compliance rates.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「垂直度偏差的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Verticality deviation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。","偏斜可能使鋼筋籠卡住或接頭形成缺口，後續即使灌足混凝土仍無法恢復原設計連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement.","Deviation can trap the cage or leave a joint gap; placing the specified concrete volume does not restore the intended continuity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"偏斜可能使鋼筋籠卡住或接頭形成缺口，後續即使灌足混凝土仍無法恢復原設計連續性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Deviation can trap the cage or leave a joint gap; placing the specified concrete volume does not restore the intended continuity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b180-v14-21","title":"槽底沉渣的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「槽底沉渣」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bottom sediment” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"成槽後的懸浮粒子會沉降在槽底，形成低強度、易壓縮的接面，也可能在混凝土置換時夾入壁體。沉渣厚度不是單靠穩定液密度可知，停置時間、粒徑及清底效果均有影響；壁樁承載與止水連續性需分別檢查。體積式只估算平均沉渣量，局部厚層可能更不利；沉渣允收需依端承、壁體品質及專案規範分別訂定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「槽底沉渣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Suspended particles settle after excavation, forming a weak compressible base or becoming trapped during concrete displacement. Slurry density alone does not establish sediment thickness; waiting time, grading and cleaning effectiveness also matter. Bearing performance of barrettes and hydraulic continuity require separate assessment of the resulting interface. The volume expression estimates mean sediment only; local thick pockets can be more adverse, and acceptance depends on bearing, wall quality and project specifications. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bottom sediment” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：槽底長L=6 m、寬B=1 m、平均沉渣厚t=0.08 m，V=L B t=0.48 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For base length L=6 m, width B=1 m and mean sediment thickness t=0.08 m, V=L B t=0.48 m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「槽底沉渣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bottom sediment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-21-k1","title":"槽底沉渣的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification","text":"成槽後的懸浮粒子會沉降在槽底，形成低強度、易壓縮的接面，也可能在混凝土置換時夾入壁體。沉渣厚度不是單靠穩定液密度可知，停置時間、粒徑及清底效果均有影響；壁樁承載與止水連續性需分別檢查。","textEn":"Suspended particles settle after excavation, forming a weak compressible base or becoming trapped during concrete displacement. Slurry density alone does not establish sediment thickness; waiting time, grading and cleaning effectiveness also matter.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「槽底沉渣的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["成槽後的懸浮粒子會沉降在槽底，形成低強度、易壓縮的接面，也可能在混凝土置換時夾入壁體。","清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。","鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。"],"optionsEn":["Suspended particles settle after excavation, forming a weak compressible base or becoming trapped during concrete displacement.","Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement.","Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"成槽後的懸浮粒子會沉降在槽底，形成低強度、易壓縮的接面，也可能在混凝土置換時夾入壁體。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Suspended particles settle after excavation, forming a weak compressible base or becoming trapped during concrete displacement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b180-v14-22","title":"槽底沉渣的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「槽底沉渣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bottom sediment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：槽底長L=6 m、寬B=1 m、平均沉渣厚t=0.08 m，V=L B t=0.48 m³。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For base length L=6 m, width B=1 m and mean sediment thickness t=0.08 m, V=L B t=0.48 m³. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在不同槽底位置量測沉渣，並核對清底與澆置間隔；用取樣及混凝土置換紀錄排查夾泥。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure sediment at multiple base positions and verify the cleaning-to-placement interval; use sampling and concrete-displacement records to investigate entrapped slurry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：槽底長L=6 m、寬B=1 m、平均沉渣厚t=0.08 m，V=L B t=0.48 m³。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For base length L=6 m, width B=1 m and mean sediment thickness t=0.08 m, V=L B t=0.48 m³. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「槽底沉渣的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。","原創教學假設：槽底長L=6 m、寬B=1 m、平均沉渣厚t=0.08 m，V=L B t=0.48 m³。","穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。"],"optionsEn":["Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight.","Original teaching assumptions: For base length L=6 m, width B=1 m and mean sediment thickness t=0.08 m, V=L B t=0.48 m³.","Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：槽底長L=6 m、寬B=1 m、平均沉渣厚t=0.08 m，V=L B t=0.48 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For base length L=6 m, width B=1 m and mean sediment thickness t=0.08 m, V=L B t=0.48 m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b180-v14-23","title":"槽底沉渣的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「槽底沉渣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bottom sediment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在不同槽底位置量測沉渣，並核對清底與澆置間隔；用取樣及混凝土置換紀錄排查夾泥。清底驗收需記錄量測位置與時間；延誤超過核定條件時由監造要求複查，不能只沿用先前合格紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure sediment at multiple base positions and verify the cleaning-to-placement interval; use sampling and concrete-displacement records to investigate entrapped slurry. Record measurement positions and time at base acceptance; delays beyond approved conditions require reinspection rather than reliance on the earlier acceptance record. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：清底驗收需記錄量測位置與時間；延誤超過核定條件時由監造要求複查，不能只沿用先前合格紀錄。體積式只估算平均沉渣量，局部厚層可能更不利；沉渣允收需依端承、壁體品質及專案規範分別訂定。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record measurement positions and time at base acceptance; delays beyond approved conditions require reinspection rather than reliance on the earlier acceptance record. The volume expression estimates mean sediment only; local thick pockets can be more adverse, and acceptance depends on bearing, wall quality and project specifications.","failure":"注意干擾：厚沉渣會造成端部壓縮或局部夾泥，表面混凝土強度合格仍可能留下深部滲漏路徑。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Thick sediment can cause base compression or slurry inclusions; satisfactory surface concrete strength does not exclude a deep leakage path. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在不同槽底位置量測沉渣，並核對清底與澆置間隔；用取樣及混凝土置換紀錄排查夾泥。清底驗收需記錄量測位置與時間；延誤超過核定條件時由監造要求複查，不能只沿用先前合格紀錄。","textEn":"Measure sediment at multiple base positions and verify the cleaning-to-placement interval; use sampling and concrete-displacement records to investigate entrapped slurry. Record measurement positions and time at base acceptance; delays beyond approved conditions require reinspection rather than reliance on the earlier acceptance record.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"清底驗收需記錄量測位置與時間；延誤超過核定條件時由監造要求複查，不能只沿用先前合格紀錄。體積式只估算平均沉渣量，局部厚層可能更不利；沉渣允收需依端承、壁體品質及專案規範分別訂定。","textEn":"Record measurement positions and time at base acceptance; delays beyond approved conditions require reinspection rather than reliance on the earlier acceptance record. The volume expression estimates mean sediment only; local thick pockets can be more adverse, and acceptance depends on bearing, wall quality and project specifications.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「槽底沉渣的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。","在不同槽底位置量測沉渣，並核對清底與澆置間隔；用取樣及混凝土置換紀錄排查夾泥。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety.","Measure sediment at multiple base positions and verify the cleaning-to-placement interval."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在不同槽底位置量測沉渣，並核對清底與澆置間隔；用取樣及混凝土置換紀錄排查夾泥。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure sediment at multiple base positions and verify the cleaning-to-placement interval; use sampling and concrete-displacement records to investigate entrapped slurry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b180-v14-24","title":"槽底沉渣的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「槽底沉渣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bottom sediment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"厚沉渣會造成端部壓縮或局部夾泥，表面混凝土強度合格仍可能留下深部滲漏路徑。體積式只估算平均沉渣量，局部厚層可能更不利；沉渣允收需依端承、壁體品質及專案規範分別訂定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Thick sediment can cause base compression or slurry inclusions; satisfactory surface concrete strength does not exclude a deep leakage path. The volume expression estimates mean sediment only; local thick pockets can be more adverse, and acceptance depends on bearing, wall quality and project specifications. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：體積式只估算平均沉渣量，局部厚層可能更不利；沉渣允收需依端承、壁體品質及專案規範分別訂定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The volume expression estimates mean sediment only; local thick pockets can be more adverse, and acceptance depends on bearing, wall quality and project specifications.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"厚沉渣會造成端部壓縮或局部夾泥，表面混凝土強度合格仍可能留下深部滲漏路徑。體積式只估算平均沉渣量，局部厚層可能更不利；沉渣允收需依端承、壁體品質及專案規範分別訂定。","textEn":"Thick sediment can cause base compression or slurry inclusions; satisfactory surface concrete strength does not exclude a deep leakage path. The volume expression estimates mean sediment only; local thick pockets can be more adverse, and acceptance depends on bearing, wall quality and project specifications.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「槽底沉渣的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bottom sediment mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["厚沉渣會造成端部壓縮或局部夾泥，表面混凝土強度合格仍可能留下深部滲漏路徑。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。"],"optionsEn":["Thick sediment can cause base compression or slurry inclusions; satisfactory surface concrete strength does not exclude a deep leakage path.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"厚沉渣會造成端部壓縮或局部夾泥，表面混凝土強度合格仍可能留下深部滲漏路徑。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Thick sediment can cause base compression or slurry inclusions; satisfactory surface concrete strength does not exclude a deep leakage path. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b180-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證」與「混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification\" and \"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b180-v14-25","title":"鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「鋼筋籠浮力」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cage buoyancy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鋼筋籠浸入穩定液後，其有效吊重因排開液體而下降，但在混凝土置換時還可能受到黏滯拖曳與上舉作用。空心附件若封閉會增加排水體積，實際浮力不一定只等於鋼筋實體體積；定位系統須辨別重量、浮力與施工擾動。阿基米德式只給靜浮力，不包括混凝土流動拖曳與卡阻；排液體積需按實際封閉附件及開口狀態計算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋼筋籠浮力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A cage immersed in slurry has reduced effective suspended weight, but concrete displacement can also create drag and upward force. Closed hollow attachments increase displaced volume, so buoyancy is not necessarily based on steel volume alone. Restraint design must distinguish weight, buoyancy and construction disturbances rather than treating every upward movement as one cause. Archimedes' expression gives static buoyancy only, excluding concrete-flow drag and snagging; displaced volume must reflect actual closed attachments and opening conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cage buoyancy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、假設總排液體積V=3 m³，浮力B=γsV=33 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: With support-fluid unit weight γs=11 kN/m³ and total displaced volume V=3 m³, buoyancy B=γsV=33 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋼筋籠浮力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cage buoyancy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-25-k1","title":"鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification","text":"鋼筋籠浸入穩定液後，其有效吊重因排開液體而下降，但在混凝土置換時還可能受到黏滯拖曳與上舉作用。空心附件若封閉會增加排水體積，實際浮力不一定只等於鋼筋實體體積；定位系統須辨別重量、浮力與施工擾動。","textEn":"A cage immersed in slurry has reduced effective suspended weight, but concrete displacement can also create drag and upward force. Closed hollow attachments increase displaced volume, so buoyancy is not necessarily based on steel volume alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。","鋼筋籠浸入穩定液後，其有效吊重因排開液體而下降，但在混凝土置換時還可能受到黏滯拖曳與上舉作用。","混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。"],"optionsEn":["Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction.","A cage immersed in slurry has reduced effective suspended weight, but concrete displacement can also create drag and upward force.","Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鋼筋籠浸入穩定液後，其有效吊重因排開液體而下降，但在混凝土置換時還可能受到黏滯拖曳與上舉作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A cage immersed in slurry has reduced effective suspended weight, but concrete displacement can also create drag and upward force. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b180-v14-26","title":"鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼筋籠浮力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cage buoyancy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、假設總排液體積V=3 m³，浮力B=γsV=33 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: With support-fluid unit weight γs=11 kN/m³ and total displaced volume V=3 m³, buoyancy B=γsV=33 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對籠體與附件體積，記錄吊重及籠頂高程，對照澆置速度與液面變化，分辨靜浮力和拖曳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check cage and attachment volumes and log suspended load and cage-top elevation against placement rate and fluid levels to distinguish static buoyancy from drag.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、假設總排液體積V=3 m³，浮力B=γsV=33 kN。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: With support-fluid unit weight γs=11 kN/m³ and total displaced volume V=3 m³, buoyancy B=γsV=33 kN. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。","穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。","原創教學假設：穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、假設總排液體積V=3 m³，浮力B=γsV=33 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members.","Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil.","Original teaching assumptions: With support-fluid unit weight γs=11 kN/m³ and total displaced volume V=3 m³, buoyancy B=γsV=33 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：穩定液γs=11 kN/m³、假設總排液體積V=3 m³，浮力B=γsV=33 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: With support-fluid unit weight γs=11 kN/m³ and total displaced volume V=3 m³, buoyancy B=γsV=33 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b180-v14-27","title":"鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼筋籠浮力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cage buoyancy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對籠體與附件體積，記錄吊重及籠頂高程，對照澆置速度與液面變化，分辨靜浮力和拖曳。澆置前由臨時工程負責人核定籠體定位與監測，任何上浮趨勢須依核定停留點處理並保存高程紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check cage and attachment volumes and log suspended load and cage-top elevation against placement rate and fluid levels to distinguish static buoyancy from drag. The temporary-works lead approves cage restraint and monitoring before placement; any rising trend is managed under an approved hold point with retained elevation records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：澆置前由臨時工程負責人核定籠體定位與監測，任何上浮趨勢須依核定停留點處理並保存高程紀錄。阿基米德式只給靜浮力，不包括混凝土流動拖曳與卡阻；排液體積需按實際封閉附件及開口狀態計算。","observationEn":"Site practice: The temporary-works lead approves cage restraint and monitoring before placement; any rising trend is managed under an approved hold point with retained elevation records. Archimedes' expression gives static buoyancy only, excluding concrete-flow drag and snagging; displaced volume must reflect actual closed attachments and opening conditions.","failure":"注意干擾：鋼筋籠上浮會改變保護層及接頭鋼筋位置，固定不足可能在混凝土開始凝結後才被發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cage uplift changes cover and connection-bar positions, and inadequate restraint may only become apparent after concrete starts setting. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對籠體與附件體積，記錄吊重及籠頂高程，對照澆置速度與液面變化，分辨靜浮力和拖曳。澆置前由臨時工程負責人核定籠體定位與監測，任何上浮趨勢須依核定停留點處理並保存高程紀錄。","textEn":"Check cage and attachment volumes and log suspended load and cage-top elevation against placement rate and fluid levels to distinguish static buoyancy from drag. The temporary-works lead approves cage restraint and monitoring before placement; any rising trend is managed under an approved hold point with retained elevation records.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"澆置前由臨時工程負責人核定籠體定位與監測，任何上浮趨勢須依核定停留點處理並保存高程紀錄。阿基米德式只給靜浮力，不包括混凝土流動拖曳與卡阻；排液體積需按實際封閉附件及開口狀態計算。","textEn":"The temporary-works lead approves cage restraint and monitoring before placement; any rising trend is managed under an approved hold point with retained elevation records. Archimedes' expression gives static buoyancy only, excluding concrete-flow drag and snagging; displaced volume must reflect actual closed attachments and opening conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對籠體與附件體積，記錄吊重及籠頂高程，對照澆置速度與液面變化，分辨靜浮力和拖曳。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Check cage and attachment volumes and log suspended load and cage-top elevation against placement rate and fluid levels to distinguish static buoyancy from drag.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對籠體與附件體積，記錄吊重及籠頂高程，對照澆置速度與液面變化，分辨靜浮力和拖曳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check cage and attachment volumes and log suspended load and cage-top elevation against placement rate and fluid levels to distinguish static buoyancy from drag. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b180-v14-28","title":"鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼筋籠浮力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cage buoyancy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鋼筋籠上浮會改變保護層及接頭鋼筋位置，固定不足可能在混凝土開始凝結後才被發現。阿基米德式只給靜浮力，不包括混凝土流動拖曳與卡阻；排液體積需按實際封閉附件及開口狀態計算。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cage uplift changes cover and connection-bar positions, and inadequate restraint may only become apparent after concrete starts setting. Archimedes' expression gives static buoyancy only, excluding concrete-flow drag and snagging; displaced volume must reflect actual closed attachments and opening conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：阿基米德式只給靜浮力，不包括混凝土流動拖曳與卡阻；排液體積需按實際封閉附件及開口狀態計算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Archimedes' expression gives static buoyancy only, excluding concrete-flow drag and snagging; displaced volume must reflect actual closed attachments and opening conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鋼筋籠上浮會改變保護層及接頭鋼筋位置，固定不足可能在混凝土開始凝結後才被發現。阿基米德式只給靜浮力，不包括混凝土流動拖曳與卡阻；排液體積需按實際封閉附件及開口狀態計算。","textEn":"Cage uplift changes cover and connection-bar positions, and inadequate restraint may only become apparent after concrete starts setting. Archimedes' expression gives static buoyancy only, excluding concrete-flow drag and snagging; displaced volume must reflect actual closed attachments and opening conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼筋籠浮力的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cage buoyancy mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","鋼筋籠上浮會改變保護層及接頭鋼筋位置，固定不足可能在混凝土開始凝結後才被發現。","混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Cage uplift changes cover and connection-bar positions, and inadequate restraint may only become apparent after concrete starts setting.","Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鋼筋籠上浮會改變保護層及接頭鋼筋位置，固定不足可能在混凝土開始凝結後才被發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cage uplift changes cover and connection-bar positions, and inadequate restraint may only become apparent after concrete starts setting. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b180-v14-29","title":"混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「混凝土量平衡」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Concrete volume balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"混凝土澆置量與理論槽體積的差異，可用於追蹤超挖、漏失或輪廓量測誤差，但過量不是品質良好的證明。澆置上升曲線若局部異常，可能反映槽壁坍落、夾泥或混凝土流入空隙，須與槽形及回收穩定液量共同判讀。此比值不區分超挖、損失及量測誤差，也沒有通用合格範圍；驗收還需材料、幾何與完整性等獨立證據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混凝土量平衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Differences between placed concrete and theoretical trench volume help track overbreak, loss and profiling error, but excess volume does not prove quality. An anomalous rise curve can indicate wall collapse, slurry entrapment or concrete entering voids and must be interpreted with trench shape and recovered-fluid volume. The ratio does not distinguish overbreak, loss and measurement error and has no universal pass range; acceptance also requires independent material, geometry and integrity evidence. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Concrete volume balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：理論體積Vt=180 m³、實際投入Va=210 m³，超量率(Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For theoretical volume Vt=180 m³ and placed volume Va=210 m³, excess ratio (Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「混凝土量平衡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Concrete volume balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-29-k1","title":"混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification","text":"混凝土澆置量與理論槽體積的差異，可用於追蹤超挖、漏失或輪廓量測誤差，但過量不是品質良好的證明。澆置上升曲線若局部異常，可能反映槽壁坍落、夾泥或混凝土流入空隙，須與槽形及回收穩定液量共同判讀。","textEn":"Differences between placed concrete and theoretical trench volume help track overbreak, loss and profiling error, but excess volume does not prove quality. An anomalous rise curve can indicate wall collapse, slurry entrapment or concrete entering voids and must be interpreted with trench shape and recovered-fluid volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。","連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。","混凝土澆置量與理論槽體積的差異，可用於追蹤超挖、漏失或輪廓量測誤差，但過量不是品質良好的證明。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall.","Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight.","Differences between placed concrete and theoretical trench volume help track overbreak, loss and profiling error, but excess volume does not prove quality."],"answer":2,"explanation":"混凝土澆置量與理論槽體積的差異，可用於追蹤超挖、漏失或輪廓量測誤差，但過量不是品質良好的證明。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Differences between placed concrete and theoretical trench volume help track overbreak, loss and profiling error, but excess volume does not prove quality. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b180-v14-30","title":"混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「混凝土量平衡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Concrete volume balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：理論體積Vt=180 m³、實際投入Va=210 m³，超量率(Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For theoretical volume Vt=180 m³ and placed volume Va=210 m³, excess ratio (Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每車方量、澆置時間與混凝土面標高形成曲線，對照超音波槽形及液體回收量，標出突變深度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot batch volume, placement time and concrete elevation, compare with ultrasonic trench profile and recovered-fluid volume, and identify depths where the trend changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：理論體積Vt=180 m³、實際投入Va=210 m³，超量率(Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For theoretical volume Vt=180 m³ and placed volume Va=210 m³, excess ratio (Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：理論體積Vt=180 m³、實際投入Va=210 m³，超量率(Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%。","穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。","槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For theoretical volume Vt=180 m³ and placed volume Va=210 m³, excess ratio (Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%.","Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level.","Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：理論體積Vt=180 m³、實際投入Va=210 m³，超量率(Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For theoretical volume Vt=180 m³ and placed volume Va=210 m³, excess ratio (Va−Vt)/Vt=16.7%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b180-v14-31","title":"混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「混凝土量平衡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Concrete volume balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每車方量、澆置時間與混凝土面標高形成曲線，對照超音波槽形及液體回收量，標出突變深度。量平衡異常須與地質及澆置事件一起審查；壁體設計者決定補充檢測範圍，不以單一超量率放行。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot batch volume, placement time and concrete elevation, compare with ultrasonic trench profile and recovered-fluid volume, and identify depths where the trend changes. Review abnormal balance together with geology and placement events; the wall designer defines supplementary investigation rather than releasing work from one excess ratio. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：量平衡異常須與地質及澆置事件一起審查；壁體設計者決定補充檢測範圍，不以單一超量率放行。此比值不區分超挖、損失及量測誤差，也沒有通用合格範圍；驗收還需材料、幾何與完整性等獨立證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Review abnormal balance together with geology and placement events; the wall designer defines supplementary investigation rather than releasing work from one excess ratio. The ratio does not distinguish overbreak, loss and measurement error and has no universal pass range; acceptance also requires independent material, geometry and integrity evidence.","failure":"注意干擾：只看總方量足夠可能掩蓋局部夾泥，過量混凝土也可能代表槽壁坍塌而非有效增加壁厚。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adequate total volume can conceal local slurry inclusions; excess concrete may indicate wall collapse rather than useful additional wall thickness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每車方量、澆置時間與混凝土面標高形成曲線，對照超音波槽形及液體回收量，標出突變深度。量平衡異常須與地質及澆置事件一起審查；壁體設計者決定補充檢測範圍，不以單一超量率放行。","textEn":"Plot batch volume, placement time and concrete elevation, compare with ultrasonic trench profile and recovered-fluid volume, and identify depths where the trend changes. Review abnormal balance together with geology and placement events; the wall designer defines supplementary investigation rather than releasing work from one excess ratio.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"量平衡異常須與地質及澆置事件一起審查；壁體設計者決定補充檢測範圍，不以單一超量率放行。此比值不區分超挖、損失及量測誤差，也沒有通用合格範圍；驗收還需材料、幾何與完整性等獨立證據。","textEn":"Review abnormal balance together with geology and placement events; the wall designer defines supplementary investigation rather than releasing work from one excess ratio. The ratio does not distinguish overbreak, loss and measurement error and has no universal pass range; acceptance also requires independent material, geometry and integrity evidence.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將每車方量、澆置時間與混凝土面標高形成曲線，對照超音波槽形及液體回收量，標出突變深度。","槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Plot batch volume, placement time and concrete elevation, compare with ultrasonic trench profile and recovered-fluid volume, and identify depths where the trend changes.","A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將每車方量、澆置時間與混凝土面標高形成曲線，對照超音波槽形及液體回收量，標出突變深度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot batch volume, placement time and concrete elevation, compare with ultrasonic trench profile and recovered-fluid volume, and identify depths where the trend changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b180-v14-32","title":"混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「混凝土量平衡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Concrete volume balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看總方量足夠可能掩蓋局部夾泥，過量混凝土也可能代表槽壁坍塌而非有效增加壁厚。此比值不區分超挖、損失及量測誤差，也沒有通用合格範圍；驗收還需材料、幾何與完整性等獨立證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adequate total volume can conceal local slurry inclusions; excess concrete may indicate wall collapse rather than useful additional wall thickness. The ratio does not distinguish overbreak, loss and measurement error and has no universal pass range; acceptance also requires independent material, geometry and integrity evidence. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此比值不區分超挖、損失及量測誤差，也沒有通用合格範圍；驗收還需材料、幾何與完整性等獨立證據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The ratio does not distinguish overbreak, loss and measurement error and has no universal pass range; acceptance also requires independent material, geometry and integrity evidence.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土用量超過理論值就代表連續壁一定更強。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Concrete volume above theory necessarily produces a stronger diaphragm wall.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看總方量足夠可能掩蓋局部夾泥，過量混凝土也可能代表槽壁坍塌而非有效增加壁厚。此比值不區分超挖、損失及量測誤差，也沒有通用合格範圍；驗收還需材料、幾何與完整性等獨立證據。","textEn":"Adequate total volume can conceal local slurry inclusions; excess concrete may indicate wall collapse rather than useful additional wall thickness. The ratio does not distinguish overbreak, loss and measurement error and has no universal pass range; acceptance also requires independent material, geometry and integrity evidence.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混凝土量平衡的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Concrete volume balance mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。","只看總方量足夠可能掩蓋局部夾泥，過量混凝土也可能代表槽壁坍塌而非有效增加壁厚。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight.","Adequate total volume can conceal local slurry inclusions; excess concrete may indicate wall collapse rather than useful additional wall thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只看總方量足夠可能掩蓋局部夾泥，過量混凝土也可能代表槽壁坍塌而非有效增加壁厚。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adequate total volume can conceal local slurry inclusions; excess concrete may indicate wall collapse rather than useful additional wall thickness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b180-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證」與「鄰房角變形的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification\" and \"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b180-v14-33","title":"接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「接頭水力坡降」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint hydraulic gradient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相鄰連續壁槽段的接頭是幾何、混凝土品質及止水構件共同形成的薄弱界面。外內水頭差沿很短的缺口集中時，局部坡降會很高，可能引發滲流帶砂；因此完工水密不是只靠壁體本身的滲透係數來判斷。坡降不是流量，仍需滲透性及路徑面積才能估算出水；局部集中流與侵蝕可能使達西均質模型失效。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接頭水力坡降」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Panel joints are interfaces governed jointly by geometry, concrete quality and sealing components. A head difference concentrated across a short defect creates a high local gradient and may transport soil. Completed-wall sealing therefore cannot be established solely from the permeability of the concrete away from its joints. Gradient is not flow rate; permeability and path area are still required, and concentrated flow or erosion may invalidate a homogeneous Darcy model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint hydraulic gradient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設水頭差Δh=10 m、有效滲流路長L=0.5 m，水力坡降i=Δh/L=20，無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For head difference Δh=10 m and effective seepage length L=0.5 m, hydraulic gradient i=Δh/L=20, dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接頭水力坡降」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint hydraulic gradient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-33-k1","title":"接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification","text":"相鄰連續壁槽段的接頭是幾何、混凝土品質及止水構件共同形成的薄弱界面。外內水頭差沿很短的缺口集中時，局部坡降會很高，可能引發滲流帶砂；因此完工水密不是只靠壁體本身的滲透係數來判斷。","textEn":"Panel joints are interfaces governed jointly by geometry, concrete quality and sealing components. A head difference concentrated across a short defect creates a high local gradient and may transport soil.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["相鄰連續壁槽段的接頭是幾何、混凝土品質及止水構件共同形成的薄弱界面。","連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。","建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。"],"optionsEn":["Panel joints are interfaces governed jointly by geometry, concrete quality and sealing components.","Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight.","Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相鄰連續壁槽段的接頭是幾何、混凝土品質及止水構件共同形成的薄弱界面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Panel joints are interfaces governed jointly by geometry, concrete quality and sealing components. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b180-v14-34","title":"接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接頭水力坡降」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint hydraulic gradient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設水頭差Δh=10 m、有效滲流路長L=0.5 m，水力坡降i=Δh/L=20，無因次。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For head difference Δh=10 m and effective seepage length L=0.5 m, hydraulic gradient i=Δh/L=20, dimensionless. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分槽段記錄水壓與出水混濁度，將接頭位置、實際偏斜及止水構件紀錄疊合，追查短路徑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record pressure and turbidity by panel, overlay joint positions, actual deviation and waterstop records, and investigate short seepage paths.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設水頭差Δh=10 m、有效滲流路長L=0.5 m，水力坡降i=Δh/L=20，無因次。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For head difference Δh=10 m and effective seepage length L=0.5 m, hydraulic gradient i=Δh/L=20, dimensionless. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["穩定液黏度足夠就一定能在任何地層形成濾餅。","原創教學假設：假設水頭差Δh=10 m、有效滲流路長L=0.5 m，水力坡降i=Δh/L=20，無因次。","地面不沉陷就表示機具載重沒有影響槽壁穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate slurry viscosity guarantees a filter cake in every soil.","Original teaching assumptions: For head difference Δh=10 m and effective seepage length L=0.5 m, hydraulic gradient i=Δh/L=20, dimensionless.","No visible surface settlement means machinery loading does not affect trench stability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設水頭差Δh=10 m、有效滲流路長L=0.5 m，水力坡降i=Δh/L=20，無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For head difference Δh=10 m and effective seepage length L=0.5 m, hydraulic gradient i=Δh/L=20, dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b180-v14-35","title":"接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接頭水力坡降」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint hydraulic gradient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分槽段記錄水壓與出水混濁度，將接頭位置、實際偏斜及止水構件紀錄疊合，追查短路徑。接頭缺陷處理需由地工及結構設計者共同核准，監測應持續涵蓋外水頭與周邊沉陷，不能只記室內漏水量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record pressure and turbidity by panel, overlay joint positions, actual deviation and waterstop records, and investigate short seepage paths. Geotechnical and structural designers jointly approve joint repair; monitoring must retain external heads and adjacent settlement rather than indoor leakage alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：接頭缺陷處理需由地工及結構設計者共同核准，監測應持續涵蓋外水頭與周邊沉陷，不能只記室內漏水量。坡降不是流量，仍需滲透性及路徑面積才能估算出水；局部集中流與侵蝕可能使達西均質模型失效。","observationEn":"Site practice: Geotechnical and structural designers jointly approve joint repair; monitoring must retain external heads and adjacent settlement rather than indoor leakage alone. Gradient is not flow rate; permeability and path area are still required, and concentrated flow or erosion may invalidate a homogeneous Darcy model.","failure":"注意干擾：接頭缺口可導致帶砂滲流與周邊沉陷；內表面止漏若未查明水路，可能只把流量轉移到鄰近界面。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A joint defect can cause sediment-carrying leakage and adjacent settlement; surface sealing without tracing the water path may merely divert flow to a neighbouring interface. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分槽段記錄水壓與出水混濁度，將接頭位置、實際偏斜及止水構件紀錄疊合，追查短路徑。接頭缺陷處理需由地工及結構設計者共同核准，監測應持續涵蓋外水頭與周邊沉陷，不能只記室內漏水量。","textEn":"Record pressure and turbidity by panel, overlay joint positions, actual deviation and waterstop records, and investigate short seepage paths. Geotechnical and structural designers jointly approve joint repair; monitoring must retain external heads and adjacent settlement rather than indoor leakage alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"接頭缺陷處理需由地工及結構設計者共同核准，監測應持續涵蓋外水頭與周邊沉陷，不能只記室內漏水量。坡降不是流量，仍需滲透性及路徑面積才能估算出水；局部集中流與侵蝕可能使達西均質模型失效。","textEn":"Geotechnical and structural designers jointly approve joint repair; monitoring must retain external heads and adjacent settlement rather than indoor leakage alone. Gradient is not flow rate; permeability and path area are still required, and concentrated flow or erosion may invalidate a homogeneous Darcy model.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","清底完成一次後，多久再澆置都不會重新沉積。","分槽段記錄水壓與出水混濁度，將接頭位置、實際偏斜及止水構件紀錄疊合，追查短路徑。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once the base is cleaned, no sediment can redeposit before concrete placement.","Record pressure and turbidity by panel, overlay joint positions, actual deviation and waterstop records, and investigate short seepage paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分槽段記錄水壓與出水混濁度，將接頭位置、實際偏斜及止水構件紀錄疊合，追查短路徑。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record pressure and turbidity by panel, overlay joint positions, actual deviation and waterstop records, and investigate short seepage paths. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b180-v14-36","title":"接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接頭水力坡降」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint hydraulic gradient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接頭缺口可導致帶砂滲流與周邊沉陷；內表面止漏若未查明水路，可能只把流量轉移到鄰近界面。坡降不是流量，仍需滲透性及路徑面積才能估算出水；局部集中流與侵蝕可能使達西均質模型失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A joint defect can cause sediment-carrying leakage and adjacent settlement; surface sealing without tracing the water path may merely divert flow to a neighbouring interface. Gradient is not flow rate; permeability and path area are still required, and concentrated flow or erosion may invalidate a homogeneous Darcy model. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：坡降不是流量，仍需滲透性及路徑面積才能估算出水；局部集中流與侵蝕可能使達西均質模型失效。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Gradient is not flow rate; permeability and path area are still required, and concentrated flow or erosion may invalidate a homogeneous Darcy model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「連續壁混凝土本體抗滲合格，就代表每個接頭水密。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Impermeable wall concrete guarantees every panel joint is watertight.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接頭缺口可導致帶砂滲流與周邊沉陷；內表面止漏若未查明水路，可能只把流量轉移到鄰近界面。坡降不是流量，仍需滲透性及路徑面積才能估算出水；局部集中流與侵蝕可能使達西均質模型失效。","textEn":"A joint defect can cause sediment-carrying leakage and adjacent settlement; surface sealing without tracing the water path may merely divert flow to a neighbouring interface. Gradient is not flow rate; permeability and path area are still required, and concentrated flow or erosion may invalidate a homogeneous Darcy model.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭水力坡降的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint hydraulic gradient mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["接頭缺口可導致帶砂滲流與周邊沉陷；內表面止漏若未查明水路，可能只把流量轉移到鄰近界面。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。"],"optionsEn":["A joint defect can cause sediment-carrying leakage and adjacent settlement.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接頭缺口可導致帶砂滲流與周邊沉陷；內表面止漏若未查明水路，可能只把流量轉移到鄰近界面。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A joint defect can cause sediment-carrying leakage and adjacent settlement; surface sealing without tracing the water path may merely divert flow to a neighbouring interface. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b180-v14-37","title":"鄰房角變形的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「鄰房角變形」如何影響連續壁槽溝穩定的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Adjacent-building distortion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Slurry-trench stability for diaphragm walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"深開挖壁體變形與地層流失可傳到鄰房，使基礎產生差異沉陷。結構反應與基礎型式、跨距及既有裂縫相關，不能用總沉陷一項代表損傷風險；角變形可作初步指標，但需扣除整體剛體傾斜並關注局部曲率。此兩點斜率不是通用損傷界限，也不能區分平移與彎曲；應增加測點、溫度修正及結構模型來辨識真實變形模式。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鄰房角變形」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wall movement and ground loss can transmit to neighbouring foundations as differential settlement. Structural response depends on foundation type, span and existing cracking, so total settlement alone does not describe damage potential. Angular distortion is an initial indicator, but rigid-body tilt must be separated and local curvature considered. This two-point slope is not a universal damage limit and cannot distinguish translation from bending; additional points, temperature corrections and structural modelling identify the real deformation mode. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Adjacent-building distortion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：兩測點差異沉陷Δs=4 mm、距離L=8 m=8000 mm，β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For differential settlement Δs=4 mm over L=8 m=8000 mm, β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad.","failure":"常見誤解：「建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鄰房角變形」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Adjacent-building distortion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-37-k1","title":"鄰房角變形的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification","text":"深開挖壁體變形與地層流失可傳到鄰房，使基礎產生差異沉陷。結構反應與基礎型式、跨距及既有裂縫相關，不能用總沉陷一項代表損傷風險；角變形可作初步指標，但需扣除整體剛體傾斜並關注局部曲率。","textEn":"Wall movement and ground loss can transmit to neighbouring foundations as differential settlement. Structural response depends on foundation type, span and existing cracking, so total settlement alone does not describe damage potential.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鄰房角變形的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。","深開挖壁體變形與地層流失可傳到鄰房，使基礎產生差異沉陷。","穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。"],"optionsEn":["Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members.","Wall movement and ground loss can transmit to neighbouring foundations as differential settlement.","Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"深開挖壁體變形與地層流失可傳到鄰房，使基礎產生差異沉陷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wall movement and ground loss can transmit to neighbouring foundations as differential settlement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b180-v14-38","title":"鄰房角變形的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鄰房角變形」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Adjacent-building distortion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：兩測點差異沉陷Δs=4 mm、距離L=8 m=8000 mm，β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For differential settlement Δs=4 mm over L=8 m=8000 mm, β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：施工前建立建物裂縫與高程基準，將精密水準、傾度及壁體位移聯合比對，檢查測點是否隨建物整體轉動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Establish preconstruction crack and elevation baselines, jointly compare precise levelling, tilt and wall movement, and determine whether points follow rigid-body building rotation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：兩測點差異沉陷Δs=4 mm、距離L=8 m=8000 mm，β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For differential settlement Δs=4 mm over L=8 m=8000 mm, β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鄰房角變形的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["槽段越長、接頭越少，就必定具有更好的整體安全性。","槽口位置正確就代表整個深槽都在設計位置。","原創教學假設：兩測點差異沉陷Δs=4 mm、距離L=8 m=8000 mm，β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad。"],"optionsEn":["Longer panels with fewer joints necessarily improve overall safety.","A correctly located trench collar guarantees the full-depth panel position.","Original teaching assumptions: For differential settlement Δs=4 mm over L=8 m=8000 mm, β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：兩測點差異沉陷Δs=4 mm、距離L=8 m=8000 mm，β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For differential settlement Δs=4 mm over L=8 m=8000 mm, β=Δs/L=0.0005 rad. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b180-v14-39","title":"鄰房角變形的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鄰房角變形」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Adjacent-building distortion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"施工前建立建物裂縫與高程基準，將精密水準、傾度及壁體位移聯合比對，檢查測點是否隨建物整體轉動。警戒值應由建物評估者依資產能力訂定；監測異常由開挖及建物設計專業共同判讀，並保留原始讀值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Establish preconstruction crack and elevation baselines, jointly compare precise levelling, tilt and wall movement, and determine whether points follow rigid-body building rotation. The building assessor sets triggers from asset capacity; excavation and building specialists interpret anomalies jointly while preserving the original measurements. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：警戒值應由建物評估者依資產能力訂定；監測異常由開挖及建物設計專業共同判讀，並保留原始讀值。此兩點斜率不是通用損傷界限，也不能區分平移與彎曲；應增加測點、溫度修正及結構模型來辨識真實變形模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: The building assessor sets triggers from asset capacity; excavation and building specialists interpret anomalies jointly while preserving the original measurements. This two-point slope is not a universal damage limit and cannot distinguish translation from bending; additional points, temperature corrections and structural modelling identify the real deformation mode.","failure":"注意干擾：若只以平均沉陷管理，局部基礎差異可能先造成梁柱裂縫；基準點受影響也會掩蓋真實變形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Managing only mean settlement can miss differential foundation movement that cracks members first; an affected survey reference can also conceal actual deformation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"施工前建立建物裂縫與高程基準，將精密水準、傾度及壁體位移聯合比對，檢查測點是否隨建物整體轉動。警戒值應由建物評估者依資產能力訂定；監測異常由開挖及建物設計專業共同判讀，並保留原始讀值。","textEn":"Establish preconstruction crack and elevation baselines, jointly compare precise levelling, tilt and wall movement, and determine whether points follow rigid-body building rotation. The building assessor sets triggers from asset capacity; excavation and building specialists interpret anomalies jointly while preserving the original measurements.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"警戒值應由建物評估者依資產能力訂定；監測異常由開挖及建物設計專業共同判讀，並保留原始讀值。此兩點斜率不是通用損傷界限，也不能區分平移與彎曲；應增加測點、溫度修正及結構模型來辨識真實變形模式。","textEn":"The building assessor sets triggers from asset capacity; excavation and building specialists interpret anomalies jointly while preserving the original measurements. This two-point slope is not a universal damage limit and cannot distinguish translation from bending; additional points, temperature corrections and structural modelling identify the real deformation mode.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鄰房角變形的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification\"?","options":["施工前建立建物裂縫與高程基準，將精密水準、傾度及壁體位移聯合比對，檢查測點是否隨建物整體轉動。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","鋼筋比穩定液重，所以施工中完全不可能上浮。"],"optionsEn":["Establish preconstruction crack and elevation baselines, jointly compare precise levelling, tilt and wall movement, and determine whether points follow rigid-body building rotation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Steel is denser than slurry, so the cage cannot rise during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工前建立建物裂縫與高程基準，將精密水準、傾度及壁體位移聯合比對，檢查測點是否隨建物整體轉動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Establish preconstruction crack and elevation baselines, jointly compare precise levelling, tilt and wall movement, and determine whether points follow rigid-body building rotation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b180-v14-40","title":"鄰房角變形的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"prerequisiteIds":["b180-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鄰房角變形」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Adjacent-building distortion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只以平均沉陷管理，局部基礎差異可能先造成梁柱裂縫；基準點受影響也會掩蓋真實變形。此兩點斜率不是通用損傷界限，也不能區分平移與彎曲；應增加測點、溫度修正及結構模型來辨識真實變形模式。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Managing only mean settlement can miss differential foundation movement that cracks members first; an affected survey reference can also conceal actual deformation. This two-point slope is not a universal damage limit and cannot distinguish translation from bending; additional points, temperature corrections and structural modelling identify the real deformation mode. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此兩點斜率不是通用損傷界限，也不能區分平移與彎曲；應增加測點、溫度修正及結構模型來辨識真實變形模式。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This two-point slope is not a universal damage limit and cannot distinguish translation from bending; additional points, temperature corrections and structural modelling identify the real deformation mode.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「建物總沉陷很小就能保證任何接縫與構件都不受損。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small total building settlement guarantees no damage to joints or members.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b180-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只以平均沉陷管理，局部基礎差異可能先造成梁柱裂縫；基準點受影響也會掩蓋真實變形。此兩點斜率不是通用損傷界限，也不能區分平移與彎曲；應增加測點、溫度修正及結構模型來辨識真實變形模式。","textEn":"Managing only mean settlement can miss differential foundation movement that cracks members first; an affected survey reference can also conceal actual deformation. This two-point slope is not a universal damage limit and cannot distinguish translation from bending; additional points, temperature corrections and structural modelling identify the real deformation mode.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]},{"id":"b180-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鄰房角變形的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Adjacent-building distortion mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若只以平均沉陷管理，局部基礎差異可能先造成梁柱裂縫；基準點受影響也會掩蓋真實變形。","穩定液密度合格就不需要再監測液面高度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Managing only mean settlement can miss differential foundation movement that cracks members first.","Acceptable slurry density eliminates the need to monitor fluid level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只以平均沉陷管理，局部基礎差異可能先造成梁柱裂縫；基準點受影響也會掩蓋真實變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Managing only mean settlement can miss differential foundation movement that cracks members first; an affected survey reference can also conceal actual deformation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-diaphragm","v14s-geo-wall","v14s-geo","b-src-geotech"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
